===============================================================================
1. WHAT THIS LICENCE COVERS
===============================================================================

This licence covers the original work in this repository, referred to below as
"the Covered Work". The Covered Work is the `wh` command line tool and its
supporting material:

  crates/        the Rust source of the tool
  docs/          the documentation and the measured protocol notes
  capture/       the traffic capture harness
  bin/           the WSL shim
  README.md, LICENSE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
  Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, .gitignore, .cargo/config.toml, and the other build
                 and configuration files at the repository root

Iain Brookes authored the Covered Work, with one exception. Parts of
`crates/wh-proto` (currently `frame.rs` and `cmds.rs`; check those files'
own module documentation, which names any file that is a port) are a Rust
port of MIT-licensed source from Sparklink Playjoy's
`@sparklinkplayjoy/protocol-keyboard` and `@sparklinkplayjoy/hid` packages,
vendored for reference at `research/proto/` and `research/hidpkg/`. Porting
code carries the licence that covers it, so the MIT notice on that upstream
source attaches to those ported portions of `crates/wh-proto` too; that
notice, and exactly what it covers, is in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Everything
else in the Covered Work, including the rest of `crates/wh-proto` that is
original rather than ported, is Iain Brookes' own authorship, and Iain
Brookes holds the copyright in it.

This licence does NOT cover the contents of `research/`, which is third-party
material owned by other people and licensed separately. See section 4 and
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

This licence does NOT cover, and asserts no claim over, anything owned by
Wallhack. See section 3.

