===============================================================================

`research/` contains third-party source vendored for reference. It is NOT part
of the Covered Work, it is NOT owned by Iain Brookes, and this licence does not
apply to it. Each item remains under its own licence, and those licences
continue to govern what you may do with it.

Nothing in section 2 restricts any right you hold under one of those licences.
Where a third-party licence grants you permission that section 2 would
otherwise withhold, that permission stands, and it applies to that third-party
material only.

This is separate from, and does not weaken, section 1's note above about the
ported portions of `crates/wh-proto`: those files are part of the Covered
Work and section 2's restrictions apply to them in full. What follows the MIT
source into the port is the attribution obligation, not a permission to
redistribute the tool; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for what that obligation
requires and how it is satisfied here.

The full list of vendored material, its origin, its licence, and the required
notices are in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Those notices are reproduced and
retained deliberately, because the licences require it.

